# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# My Maestro AI — Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env

# ── API Keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI provider and web-search keys are not kept in this file. Enter them on the Welcome page or in
# Settings → AI models; they are saved in data/settings.json, readable only by your account.
# A line like OPENAI_API_KEY=… here (also ANTHROPIC_, GEMINI_, PERPLEXITY_, OPENROUTER_API_KEY and BRAVE_SEARCH_,
# SERPER_, TAVILY_API_KEY) is moved into Settings when the hub starts, and the old file is kept as .env.bak-<time>. To keep keys in this file instead, set HUB_KEEP_ENV_KEYS=1.

# ── User Identity ────────────────────────────────────────────
USER_EMAIL=your@email.com
SLACK_USER_ID=YOUR_SLACK_USER_ID

# ── Web UI Auth (optional) ───────────────────────────────────
# Legacy single-password login: used only while the hub has no accounts. With accounts it is ignored; network
# exposure then needs an admin with two-factor, and scripts or bots sign in with API tokens (Users page).
# HUB_AUTH_USERNAME=
# HUB_AUTH_PASSWORD=

# ── Network binding ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The hub listens on 127.0.0.1 ONLY by default. To reach it from other
# machines, set HUB_BIND_HOST (e.g. 0.0.0.0 or a specific LAN address).
# This is honoured ONLY when BOTH auth values above are set; otherwise it
# is ignored and the hub stays on localhost.
# HUB_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0

# ── Tailnet access (scripts/tailscale-setup.sh) ──────────────
# Extra hostnames the hub accepts from browsers besides localhost and Tailscale
# names (*.ts.net need no entry), e.g. a reverse proxy's name.
# HUB_ALLOWED_HOSTS=hub.example.com
# Tailscale logins allowed through Serve (comma-separated). Unset = no gate.
# Direct localhost requests are always allowed.
# HUB_TAILNET_USERS=you@example.com

# ── Agent permissions ────────────────────────────────────────
# acceptEdits (default) or bypassPermissions. bypassPermissions lets agents run
# any tool on this machine without prompting: trusted single-user installs only.
# HUB_AGENT_PERMISSION_MODE=acceptEdits
# Default tool scope for spawn_workers when the caller gives none: read (default), full, none.
# HUB_WORKER_DEFAULT_SCOPE=read

# ── MCP Skills (optional — configure via setup wizard) ───────

# GitHub
# GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_HOST=github.com

# Slack (token stored at ~/.config/slack-mcp/token after OAuth)

# PagerDuty
# PAGERDUTY_API_TOKEN=

# Datadog
# DD_APPLICATION_KEY=

# Splunk
# SPLUNK_HOST=
# SPLUNK_TOKEN=

# Sourcegraph
# SOURCEGRAPH_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Claude Agent SDK (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# The hub auto-selects the NEWEST @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk installed
# anywhere on this machine (hub node_modules or npm global). To pin a
# specific copy instead, point this at the package directory:
# CLAUDE_SDK_PATH=/path/to/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk

# ── Local LLM (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# LM_STUDIO_URL=http://localhost:4000/v1
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
